Ask for forward error correction on video and rebuild lost packets.

Current Steam sends video with FEC when the client sets enable_unreliable_fec (field 25 of
CStreamingClientConfig). The format, worked out from captured traffic and described in
session/fec.h: each message goes out under one packet id as UnreliableFEC packets (type 11),
k data shards and m parity shards, the fragment id being the shard index. Parity shard r is
the sum of d_i / (r + m + i) over GF(2^8), polynomial 0x11d, + being XOR: a Cauchy matrix.
Steam used m = 1, and m = 2 for messages above about 30 KB. All 6074 parity rows in two
captures matched, and replaying the captures with drops (up to every third large shard)
rebuilt every message that had at most m shards missing, byte for byte.

IHS_SessionFECAdd reassembles the shards of up to 32 messages in flight and hands each
complete or rebuilt message to the window as a plain Unreliable packet, so the rest of the
data path is unchanged. A message that loses more than m shards is lost as before (skipped,
keyframe request). IHS_SessionConfig.enableFec turns it on. A host that doesn't know the
field ignores it, as protobuf does, and plain packets are still handled. Without this patch
the header parser rejected type 11, so turning FEC on meant no video at all. The stream stats
gain fec, fecRecovered and fecUnrecoverable.

